// Fork: the ONE signing setting for `make testflight` that needs SDK-scoping.
//
// The GRDB macro plugin and the SwiftLint/SwiftGen build tools are macOS
// command-line tools. If they inherit the iOS app's entitlements (app-group /
// iCloud) via the global CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS override, the signed macro plugin
// emits junk on its stdio pipe and the compiler fails the archive with
// "external macro ... produced malformed response".
//
// Plain command-line KEY=value overrides can't be scoped per-SDK, so disabling
// signing for macOS hosts (which are build-time only and never shipped) lives here
// and is applied via `xcodebuild -xcconfig`. Everything else stays as command-line
// overrides in the Makefile so paths resolve absolutely across SPM package targets.
CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED[sdk=macosx*] = NO
